.TH CADO.CONF 5 "August 23, 2026" "VirtualSquare Labs"
.SH NAME
cado.conf \- cado capability authorization configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I /etc/cado.conf
defines which ambient capabilities cado may delegate. The complete file is
validated before any authorization is returned. A malformed noncomment entry
prints a file-and-line diagnostic and causes the file to fail closed.
.PP
Blank lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is
.B #
are ignored. Every other line is exactly one of:
.nf
    capability-list : principal-list
    capability-list : principal-list : condition-sequence
.fi
Extra fields and empty required fields are invalid.
.SH CAPABILITIES
.I capability-list
is comma-separated. An item is a libcap capability name, with or without
.BR cap_ ,
or an unsigned unprefixed hexadecimal mask. Surrounding whitespace is trimmed.
Empty lists/items, signs,
.B 0x
prefixes, overflow, trailing text, and bits above the supported Linux
capability range are rejected.
.SH PRINCIPALS
.I principal-list
is a nonempty comma-separated list. An item is a username or a group name
prefixed by
.BR @ .
Empty and whitespace-containing identifiers are invalid.
.SH CONDITIONS
.I condition-sequence
is executed only for a matching identity and relevant capability entry, using
libexecs 1.4's sequence API. Environment variables are expanded. The condition
child first drops ambient capabilities. A nonzero condition result denies that
entry; callback failures therefore deny it as well.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
    # Capability Ambient DO configuration
    net_admin: @netadmin,renzo
    cap_kill: renzo
    setgid,setuid: giovanni: /usr/bin/logger cado identity caps for $USER
    c0: giovanni,@idgroup
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cado.conf
Protected system authorization configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cado (1),
.BR scado (1),
.BR capabilities (7)
